This line directly writes the user-provided `busy_poll_to` value (converted to nanoseconds) into the context without any upper bound. A large or unbounded value causes the NAPI polling loop to run for an excessive duration without conditional rescheduling, leading to kernel complaints about a stuck task.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
napi->busy_poll_to = min(10000, napi->busy_poll_to);
WRITE_ONCE(ctx->napi_busy_poll_dt, napi->busy_poll_to * NSEC_PER_USEC);
Reason:
The `min()` caps `busy_poll_to` to 10 milliseconds (10000 microseconds) before it is written to the context. This limits the polling duration to a sane value, preventing the loop from running too long and avoiding kernel preemption complaints.

